'' RUN: two copies in the runtime that had no bound (security review, Nov 2026). PRINT USING's
'' string field -- a backslash, blanks, a backslash -- is as wide as the format says, and one
'' wider than the 2048-character buffer wrote the string, or its padding, past it on the
'' stack: the field is held to the buffer. And OPEN COM copied the device name before its ':'
'' into 128 bytes whatever its length: a name that does not fit is error 1.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/rt-field-bounds.bas -o tests/codegen/rtfieldbounds.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/rtfieldbounds.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: long 2048
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: short 2048
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: com 1
